{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1352020,"ns":0,"title":"Fudge factor","extract":"A fudge factor is an ad hoc quantity or element introduced into a calculation, formula or model in order to make it fit observations or expectations.  Also known as a correction coefficient, which is defined by\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          κ\n          \n            c\n          \n        \n        =\n        \n          \n            experimental value\n            theoretical value\n          \n        \n        .","description":"Ad hoc element introduced into a calculation","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}